From: SolidWorks Maker on Mac
Subject: winemac.drv: show GDI-presented GL frames immediately; optional sRGB windows

With SW_OPENGL_GDI=1, each OpenGL frame is copied into the window's GDI surface.
win32u only flushes a surface when the app goes idle, or every 50 ms while it stays
busy, so view rotation was capped near 20-24 fps. Flush the toplevel surface right
after each presented frame (plain opaque surfaces only). SW_OPENGL_GDI_FLUSH=0
restores the old behavior.

SW_MAC_SRGB=1 gives new Cocoa windows an sRGB backing store, matching Wine's sRGB
GDI images, so Core Animation no longer converts every pixel on the CPU.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -1079,6 +1079,12 @@
 
         if (!window) return nil;
 
+        /* GDI surface images are 8-bit sRGB. Matching the window backing color space
+         * avoids a CPU conversion of every pixel when Core Animation copies the image;
+         * ColorSync still maps the window to the display. Opt-in: SW_MAC_SRGB=1. */
+        if ([[[NSProcessInfo processInfo] environment][@"SW_MAC_SRGB"] boolValue])
+            [window setColorSpace:[NSColorSpace sRGBColorSpace]];
+
         /* Standardize windows to eliminate differences between titled and
            borderless windows and between NSWindow and NSPanel. */
         [window setHidesOnDeactivate:NO];
